---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
---

<section id="about">
  <Image
    src="https://github.com/josmrpy/josmrpy/raw/main/banner.png"
    class="about-banner"
    alt="Josimar Madrigal (josmr.py) profile banner"
    width={1200}
    height={300}
    format="webp"
    loading="lazy"
  />
  <h2>About me</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    A bit about me, my interests, and what drives me to build and contribute.
  </p>
  <div class="about-shell">
    <div class="about-photo-slot">
      <Image
        class="about-photo"
        src="https://github.com/josmrpy.png"
        alt="Josimar Madrigal"
        width={256}
        height={256}
        format="webp"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p class="about-bio">
        I'm a Costa Rican student finishing a technical diploma in Network
        Configuration, Communications Support and Operating Systems at CTP
        Limón. I'm deeply interested in computer science and programming, and I
        like getting involved in things where I can learn, build, and
        contribute. I often end up turning that curiosity into projects of my
        own — from an AAC app and small platforms to a sumo-fighting robot and
        simple tools built to solve everyday problems. I'm also drawn to
        intercultural experiences, civic projects, and youth leadership, and I
        enjoy getting involved in communities and initiatives beyond the
        classroom.
      </p>
      <p class="about-bio">
        What ties most of it together is a simple idea: technology is most
        interesting to me when it can solve a real problem. I'm particularly
        interested in accessibility and civic participation, where software and
        technical skills can make information, communication, and opportunities
        easier to reach.
      </p>
      <dl class="quick-facts">
        <div>
          <dt>Based in</dt>
          <dd>Limón, Costa Rica</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Education</dt>
          <dd>CTP Limón — Networks &amp; Operating Systems, Dec 2026</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Languages</dt>
          <dd>Spanish (native) · English (B2)</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>What I do</dt>
          <dd>
            Programming · Building projects · Technology · Intercultural
            experiences · Civic engagement
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
